DesignWare I2C: release every reset the node names, not only the first. The
AX620E has an APB and a core reset per controller; either one left asserted
holds the block. The binding's resets maxItems 1 is exceeded on purpose.

--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c
@@ -236,7 +236,7 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	dev->rst = devm_reset_control_get_optional_exclusive(device, NULL);
+	dev->rst = devm_reset_control_array_get_optional_exclusive(device);
 	if (IS_ERR(dev->rst))
 		return dev_err_probe(device, PTR_ERR(dev->rst), "failed to acquire reset\n");
 
